  "notes": "Godan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), る-ending (godan, not ichidan).\n- Negative: {取|と}り{去|さ}らない\n- Polite: {取|と}り{去|さ}ります\n- Te-form: {取|と}り{去|さ}って\n- Past: {取|と}り{去|さ}った\n\nUSAGE:\nEmphasizes complete removal with nothing left behind. Can be used both for physical removal (stains, objects) and abstract elimination (fears, obstacles). Somewhat more literary than {取|と}り{除|のぞ}く.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- シミを{取|と}り{去|さ}る: to remove a stain\n- {汚|よご}れを{取|と}り{去|さ}る: to remove dirt\n- {不安|ふあん}を{取|と}り{去|さ}る: to eliminate anxiety\n- {障害|しょうがい}を{取|と}り{去|さ}る: to remove an obstacle\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{取|と}り{去|さ}る emphasizes complete removal. {取|と}り{除|のぞ}く (to remove, to get rid of) is more common in everyday speech. {取|と}り{払|はら}う (to clear away) emphasizes clearing or sweeping away.",
